WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.560
In 1964, Britain carried
out its last executions.

2
00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:08.830
In 1965, the death penalty
for murder was abolished.

3
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.840
Yet some countries, such as
China, Iran and Saudi Arabia,

4
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:16.040
still use it, as do some US states.

5
00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.700
So can a state ever be right to
put someone to death for a crime?

6
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:24.000
In this mission, you'll weigh
arguments from retribution,

7
00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:27.820
deterrence, utility and
the sanctity of life.

8
00:00:27.870 --> 00:00:30.900
Then you'll trace how
Catholic teaching has changed,

9
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:34.890
and hear what Humanists and other
non-religious thinkers argue.

10
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:40.040
Your mission: weigh up both sides, and
explain why believers and non-believers

11
00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:40.910
disagree.
